  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in account ACC-1005 (EUR):\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Direction:** Outgoing card payment\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nI also see a second payment to the same merchant for the same amount, TX-0402 (EUR 240.00, 2026-07-14, settled). You haven't said what happened, so I'm not drawing a conclusion from that, but it's the first thing to check if you think you were charged twice.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes Verta supports, and what each one covers:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** The same purchase was charged more than once. This could fit if TX-0401 and TX-0402 were for one order.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** You did not authorize the payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** A card payment was made without your card being present, such as an online transaction you did not make.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid for something and did not receive it.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nTell me which situation matches, and I'll check whether a dispute is eligible for TX-0401 under that code before anything is filed. Opening a dispute is irreversible, so I won't file one without your confirmation.",
